  {
    "issue": "Hunter.io returns no email found, or usable is always False",
    "fix": "The free tier has a monthly search cap and doesn't cover every domain - this is expected for some prospects, not a bug. Have a manual-entry fallback ready, and check hunter.py's MIN_CONFIDENCE (50) isn't being compared against a None score (find_email() already handles that case)."
  },
  {
    "issue": "AI request failed: No AI provider configured",
    "fix": "Add either AI_PROVIDER=gemini plus GEMINI_API_KEY=... (free, from aistudio.google.com/apikey), or AI_PROVIDER=claude plus ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... (from console.anthropic.com/settings/keys) to your .env file, in the same folder as sdt_ai.py."
  },
  {
    "issue": "LinkedIn-related searches get blocked or return nothing",
    "fix": "This project searches for a prospect's public presence via Tavily rather than scraping LinkedIn directly, specifically to avoid this - but Tavily's own results can still be thin for a low-profile person. Treat empty profile results as best-effort and fall back to company news alone."
  },
  {
    "issue": "write_email.py raises ValueError: 'The AI used a banned generic filler phrase'",
    "fix": "This is the guard working as designed, not a bug - review the printed email and either send it after removing the phrase by hand, or call write_cold_email() again (models are non-deterministic, a second attempt often avoids the same phrase)."
  },
  {
    "issue": "The cold email reads like a generic template with names swapped in",
    "fix": "Double check the actual researched details (recent_event, challenges) are reaching build_prompt() in write_email.py - not a placeholder or empty value from a failed enrich_prospect() call. A generic-sounding email is usually a symptom of empty context, not a prompting problem."
  },
  {
    "issue": "sequence.py raises ValueError: 'Sequence is missing day(s)'",
    "fix": "Run build_followup_sequence() again - this usually fixes itself. If it keeps happening, the prompt in sequence.py's build_prompt() may need the day-3/7/14 requirement stated even more explicitly."
  }
